,568</div></div></div><div class="prose" style="font-size:14px;margin-top:16px">The asking price of $8,900 is above the $6,928-$7,568 range these comparable listings support after the deductions above. The gap is $1,332.</div><div style="margin-top:20px"><div class="mono-label">The comps behind this range</div><table style="margin-top:8px"><thead><tr><th>Listing</th><th>Year / trim</th><th>Mileage</th><th>Asking</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year, LX trim</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>112,300</td><td>$9,400</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>134,800</td><td>$8,100</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - listing 40 miles away, lower mileage</td><td>2013 EX</td><td>98,500</td><td>$10,200</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - high-mileage example, same trim</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>151,000</td><td>$7,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin-top:20px"><div class="mono-label">Deductions, each linked to a finding</div><table style="margin-top:8px"><tbody><tr><td><a href="#vf_rust_01">Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</a></td><td style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">-$600 to -$900</td><td class="muted prose" style="font-size:12px">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.72.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vf_tire_01">Front left tread appears low</a></td><td style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">-$380 to -$620</td><td class="muted prose" style="font-size:12px">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.58.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:18px">Mileage adjustment of $-0.056 per mile, fitted from the 4 comparable listings provided rather than from any assumed depreciation rate. Range built from 4 listing(s) you provided. It reflects those listings and nothing else - not a market index, not an appraisal. Asking prices, not sale prices. What a car is listed at and what it sells for are different numbers, and the second one is not public. Subject mileage of 128,540 is as stated by the seller and has not been verified.</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Questions for the seller</div><ol class="prose" style="padding-left:22px;font-size:14px"><li style="margin-bottom:8px">How long has the rust on the rocker panel been there, and has any bodywork been done to it?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Do you know how the dent on the rear quarter happened?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">The check-engine light is on in your photo. What code is it throwing, and how long has it been on?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Can you show me the title and any service records so I can check the mileage history?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">How old are the tires, and were they all replaced at the same time?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Is the engine losing any fluid? When were the fluids last topped up or changed?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Has recall FIX000002 been performed? A dealer will do it free - ask for the paperwork.</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Do you have service records? Can I see them before I come out?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Has this car been in any accident, reported or not?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Are you the titleholder, and is the title in hand and clear?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Can I take it to my mechanic for a pre-purchase inspection?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Can you show me the dealer paperwork for the open recalls on this VIN?</li></ol></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Negotiation script</div><div style="display:grid;gap:12px"><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Open by naming what you did</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I ran the photos and the VIN through an AI analysis before coming out. It flagged a few things I want to look at with you.”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Raise: Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis flagged corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel. I&#x27;d want that looked at - a shop quoted that kind of work at roughly $600 to $900. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Raise: Front left tread appears low</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis flagged front left tread appears low. I&#x27;d want that looked at - a shop quoted that kind of work at roughly $380 to $620. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Anchor on the comps</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I looked at comparable listings and they support roughly $6,928 to $7,568 for this car in this condition. Here are the listings I looked at. Can you meet me in that range?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Protect yourself on what the analysis could not see</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis was clear that it can&#x27;t assess brakes, airbags, frame, or steering from photos. I&#x27;d like to take it to my mechanic before we finalize. If that&#x27;s not possible, I understand, but then I&#x27;d need the price to reflect the risk I&#x27;m taking on.”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Be willing to leave</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I appreciate your time. Let me think it over and I&#x27;ll call you tomorrow.”</div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Run metadata</div><table><tbody><tr><td class="mono-label">Mode</td><td>fixture</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Images analyzed</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Tokens</td><td>0 in / 0 out</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Audio processed</td><td>22.0s</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Cost to produce</td><td style="color:var(--tk-accent)">$0.0000</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Note</td><td class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px">Fixture mode: responses served from cache, no API calls billed. $0.00 is the true cost of this run and not a placeholder.</td></tr></tbody></table></section><footer style="margin-top:72px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--tk-line);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:11px"><span class="mono-label">INSPECTED BY TIREKICK AI</span><span class="muted prose" style="max-width:620px">Automated analysis of buyer-supplied media. Not an inspection. Have an independent mechanic examine any vehicle before you buy it. <a href="/accuracy">Accuracy and known limits</a>.</span></footer></div>"`;
